# At-directive disambiguation

Bare names are directives only when registered: @span renders an (empty) span,
but @unknown stays literal text.

An `@` glued to a word is prose, never a directive — user@span — and a real
email like me@host.com still autolinks.

A bracket form is a directive anywhere it appears: @span[hi].

A `+`-block directive is an error if it does not start its own line:
a stray @callout+[oops] mid-paragraph is flagged.
